        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "We have presented a preliminary framework for detecting SGWB for Taiji mission. The code used in this work is publicly available at https://github.com/DrizzleatDusk/TaijiSGWB. The present work focuses on the official Taiji training datasets, which incorporate realistic features such as unequal noise levels and time-varying armlengths. We show that applying an equal-arm model to the flexing-arm datasets introduces significant bias. To address this, we segment time-domain strain data and compute the detector response individually for each segment, subsequently evaluating the likelihood via inversion of the full, non-diagonal covariance matrix.",
            "block_bbox": [
                101,
                1287,
                1127,
                1425
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
